# Binary files git must never touch.
#
# Without this, a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# LF byte inside a PDF or an Office document into CRLF, and the file arrives
# corrupt. It commits intact, which is what makes it easy to miss: the damage
# happens on the CLIENT's checkout, not on ours.
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
